ternational legal work requires comparing multiple legal systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Study differences between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"India"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"US"},{"text":"EU jurisdictions"},{"text":"Singapore"},{"text":"UAE"},{"text":"Other relevant commercial jurisdictions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Compare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Corporate law"},{"text":"Arbitration"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Competition"},{"text":"Investment"},{"text":"Dispute resolution"},{"text":"The objective is to understand how legal rules interact across jurisdictions, not merely memorize foreign statutes."}]}]},{"heading":"Language & Cross-Cultural Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"International legal work benefits greatly from:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional English"},{"text":"Legal writing"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Stakeholder management"},{"text":"Additional foreign-language knowledge can be advantageous depending on the target region."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential languages include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"French"},{"text":"German"},{"text":"Spanish"},{"text":"Arabic"},{"text":"Mandarin"},{"text":"Japanese"},{"text":"Language is an advantage, not a universal requirement."}]}]},{"heading":"Digital & Legal Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Legal research platforms"},{"text":"Document-management systems"},{"text":"PDF tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transaction Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Virtual data rooms"},{"text":"Contract lifecycle management"},{"text":"Document comparison"},{"text":"E-signature platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Legal matter dashboards"}]}]},{"heading":"AI for International Legal Work","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treaty comparison"},{"text":"Cross-border document review"},{"text":"Contract summarization"},{"text":"Case-law organization"},{"text":"Multijurisdictional research"},{"text":"Translation assistance"},{"text":"Due diligence"},{"text":"Regulatory monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Responsible Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["International Legal Question","AI-Assisted Research","Potential Authorities","Verify Actual Sources","Check Jurisdiction & Date","Compare Legal Systems","Human Legal Analysis","Final Advice"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated international-law authorities, treaty provisions and citations must always be independently verified."}]},{"heading":"Projects During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — International Treaty Database"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a database containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treaty name"},{"text":"Subject"},{"text":"Participating countries"},{"text":"Date"},{"text":"Status"},{"text":"Relevant obligations"},{"text":"Dispute mechanism"},{"text":"Domestic implementation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Cross-Border Contract Review"},{"type":"p","text":"Review a fictional international commercial agreement."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Governing law"},{"text":"Jurisdiction"},{"text":"Arbitration"},{"text":"Currency"},{"text":"Tax"},{"text":"IP"},{"text":"Data"},{"text":"Sanctions"},{"text":"Termination"},{"text":"Liability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — International Arbitration Simulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a mock dispute:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Commercial Contract","Dispute","Notice of Arbitration","Jurisdictional Issues","Claim","Defence","Evidence","Hearing","Award"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Comparative Law Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare the legal treatment of one issue across:"},{"type":"flow","items":["India","UK","US","Singapore"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a structured research report."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — International Trade Compliance Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a dashboard tracking:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Countries"},{"text":"Products/services"},{"text":"Regulatory requirements"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Trade restrictions"},{"text":"Contract status"},{"text":"Compliance risks"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Best Internship Environments"},{"type":"table","header":["Environment","Exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"International Law Firm"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Arbitration Practice"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"International Trade Team"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Corporate Law Firm"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"International Organization"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Human Rights Organization"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Policy Think Tank"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"International NGO"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Government International Affairs Body"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"In-House Multinational Legal Team"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Arbitration Centre"},{"text":"High"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Legal Research","International Legal Research","Treaty Research","Contract Review","Arbitration Research","Cross-Border Transaction Support","International Legal Advisory"]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"International Law"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public international law"},{"text":"Private international law"},{"text":"Treaty law"},{"text":"International organizations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Arbitration"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International commercial arbitration"},{"text":"Arbitration procedure"},{"text":"Mediation"},{"text":"Alternative dispute resolution"}]},{