esolution"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"International Compliance"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Human Rights"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"International Environmental Law"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Cross-Cultural Communication"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Policy Analysis"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Legal Technology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AI-Assisted International Legal Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["LLB","International Law Specialization","International Law/Arbitration Internship","Treaty + Cross-Border Contract + Dispute Research","Junior International Legal Role","International Law Consultant","Senior Specialist","International Counsel / Policy Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"For the International Law → International Law Consultant pathway, the strongest candidate combines international legal knowledge with a specific marketable specialization such as arbitration, international trade, investment law, human rights or cross-border transactions. An LLB provides the foundation, but international internships, strong legal research, comparative-law skills, professional writing, negotiation and genuine cross-border exposure are what make the profile competitive."}]}]}